    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a stiff challenge today against Williams, G, whose 2.95 xERA forces us to exercise extreme caution with our offensive output. Given the high-caliber pitching, only **Sam Antonacci** manages to clear our efficiency threshold with a score of 47.20. While the SP skill penalty is heavy at -19%, **Sam Antonacci** benefits significantly from his leadoff spot and a positive platoon adjustment, keeping him as our most viable play. **Miguel Vargas** remains in the mix at 40.40, surviving the benching threshold by the narrowest of margins; while his base projection is solid, the matchup against Williams, G and a negative adjustment for the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time suppress his ceiling, making him a marginal start that we are relying on to avoid a total collapse.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was keeping **Brayan Rocchio** on the bench with a score of 38.59. While he demonstrated strong recent form, his placement at the bottom of the order and the opposing pitcher's respectable 3.79 xERA created a mathematical drag that pushed him just below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" We are playing for efficiency today, and in a 5x5 Roto environment where we need to maximize every plate appearance, we cannot afford to gamble on low-order hitters against capable arms. Elsewhere, our core\u2014including **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2014remains unavailable due to team off-days or injury status, leaving us light on high-end production. We will continue to monitor the status of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Franklin Arias** for future deployment, but today, patience remains our primary strategy.",
